- Requiting Hex ({B})\n\
- Spell Snare ({U})\n\
- Three Steps Ahead ({U})\n\
- Consult the Star Charts ({1}{U})\n\
\n\
All of these are playable with my current mana.\n\
\n\
As a Johnny, I love setting up clever lines. Let’s evaluate:\n\
\n\
- Requiting Hex is a 1/1 with morbid — if a creature died this turn, it becomes a 3/3. But nothing has died yet, so I’d be getting a 1/1 for 1B, which is underwhelming.\n\
- Spell Snare could counter an important 2-mana spell, but it’s a reactive card — I’d rather hold it for now.\n\
- Three Steps Ahead lets me look at the top two cards and put one in my hand — great for setting up future turns, but I’m not under pressure yet, and it doesn’t develop my board.\n\
- Consult the Star Charts ({1}{U}) lets me look at the top four cards and rearrange them. That’s a strong card for a control or combo-leaning deck — perfect for my Johnny style. It helps me find more gas, set up draws, and smooth my draws. I should cast this now to dig for better cards while maintaining tempo.\n\
\n\
I’ll lead with Consult the Star Charts to improve my hand and set up future plays.\n\
\n\
I have enough mana:\n\
- Tap Island for {U}\n\
- Tap Swamp for {B}, but I need {1} colorless and {U}\n\
- So I need one more mana.\n\
\n\
Wait — I only have two lands. I can’t pay {1}{U} unless I have another source. I only have {B} and {U} available — no way to generate a colorless {1}. So I can’t cast Consult the Star Charts yet.\n\
\n\
That means the only spells I can cast are:\n\
- Requiting Hex: {B} — yes, I can cast.\n\
- Spell Snare: {U} — yes.\n\
- Three Steps Ahead: {U} — yes.\n\
\n\
Among these, Requiting Hex is the only permanent I can play. But for 1B, a 1/1 without morbid is weak — I’d rather not telegraph my graveyard synergy if I don’t need to. Holding Spell Snare or Three Steps Ahead might be better.\n\
\n\
But as a Johnny, I like setting up sequences — and Three Steps Ahead can help me see what’s coming, so I can plan a cool interaction.\n\
\n\
I can cast Three Steps Ahead for {U}. No downside — it’s an instant, and it helps me plan my next turns.\n\
\n\
So I’ll cast Three Steps Ahead.\n\
\n\
I only need {U} — I’ll tap Island to pay.\n\
