      "reasoning": "Turn 4 — my turn.\n\
\n\
I untapped, drew a card (now 7 in hand), and entered main phase.\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- Two untapped lands: Island, Gloomlake Verge\n\
- Can play one more land: Watery Grave (p9)\n\
\n\
I can cast:\n\
- Consult the Star Charts (p5 or p12): {1}{U} — can kick with {1}{U} if I have mana\n\
- Bitter Triumph (p4): {1}{B} — I can pay with Gloomlake → {B}, and Island or Gloom for {1}\n\
- Three Steps Ahead: {U} plus additional cost — min {2}{U} total — not enough\n\
\n\
First, play Watery Grave (p9).\n\
\n\
I can have it enter untapped by paying 2 life or returning a non-Island.\n\
\n\
I have only one Island — if I return it, I lose blue source.\n\
\n\
I have Gloomlake Verge, which can produce U — so I can return Island and still have U source.\n\
\n\
But why bother? I can just pay 2 life.\n\
\n\
I'm at 20 — losing 2 is fine.\n\
\n\
So I'll pay 2 life to have Watery Grave enter untapped.\n\
\n\
Now I have three untapped lands: all producing U or B.\n\
\n\
Then I can cast something.\n\
\n\
Best to cast Consult the Star Charts with kicker.\n\
\n\
Cost: {2}{U}\n\
- I have three lands, can tap two for {U} and one for {1}, or use Gloom for {U}, Watery for {U}, and Island for {1}\n\
\n\
Perfect.\n\
\n\
So:\n\
- Play Watery Grave, pay 2 life\n\
- Cast Consult the Star Charts kicked\n\
\n\
I'll do that.\n\
\n\
First, play Watery Grave.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
