      "reasoning": "Ah, the state is now clear.\n\
\n\
We are at the start of **Turn 5**, **Sarge's turn**, and **Three Steps Ahead is still in our hand** — meaning our attempt to cast it failed earlier due to the mana plan error.\n\
\n\
Our last cast — **Consult the Star Charts** — resolved successfully. We looked at the top 3 cards of our library (because we control 3 lands), and chose to put **Fountainport** into our hand. The rest — Stock Up and Three Steps Ahead — were put on the bottom in an order we chose (likely Fountainport on top, then the other two beneath).\n\
\n\
But now we're back in Sarge's turn, so we must have passed priority after resolving Consult the Star Charts.\n\
\n\
Now, **we have another chance** — Three Steps Ahead is back in hand, and it's still our turn coming up.\n\
\n\
Let’s play smart.\n\
\n\
We should cast **Three Steps Ahead** on **our** turn, not wait. We’re at 18 life, no immediate pressure, and we want maximum value.\n\
\n\
But first — Sarge is currently in their **precombat main phase**, and they just played an **additional Steam Vents** and cast **Ral, Crackling Wit** (a 1-loyalty planeswalker).\n\
\n\
We need to **hold up counterspells**.\n\
\n\
Ral, Crackling Wit can:\n\
- **+1**: Draw a card, then clash — if you win, draw two more. So minimum +1 card, potentially +3.\n\
- Can also **-3** to deal 2 damage to any target and draw a card.\n\
\n\
We should be careful — Ral could grow fast.\n\
\n\
But for now, our plan:\n\
\n\
1. Wait and see if Sarge makes a move we want to counter.\n\
2. On **our** turn, cast **Three Steps Ahead** to dig deeper.\n\
3. Then look for ways to chain card draw and set up a combo or control loop.\n\
\n\
Three Steps Ahead is **free to cast**, and we have **Spell Snare** and **Spell Pierce** — perfect for countering a 2- or 3-mana spell.\n\
\n\
Let’s hold them.\n\
\n\
So — for now, **pass priority** and let Sarge finish their turn.\n\
\n\
We’ll set a stop at **end_of_turn** to skip to our turn.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
