    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With only 3 lands and the opponent having Ral, Crackling Wit on the battlefield (a must-answer threat that generates incremental advantage), casting Stock Up as a sorcery taps out all 3 mana during the main phase. This leaves no mana open to interact with the opponent on their turn - no Spell Pierce, no Spell Snare, no Requiting Hex to kill the Otter token, and no Three Steps Ahead to counter anything. The player has Requiting Hex which can kill the 1/1 Otter token for just B (with Gloomlake Verge available), and could hold up countermagic for Ral's follow-up plays. Stock Up is a card advantage spell but it's a sorcery that taps out when the opponent has an active planeswalker generating value. The player should be prioritizing interaction over card draw at this stage.",
